; NextDAAD accented-glyph fixture (2026-08-30). Compiled and
; byte-asserted by testsuild-tests.ps1 on every run; -Accent stages
; it into sd\ACCENT\. Drives DRC's two accent encodings against the
; charset redirect in src\print.asm (prn_shift): encoding 1 = bare
; bytes 16-31, encoding 2 = $0E chr(16..31) $0F triples reaching
; glyphs 144-159, sharp-s = a DIRECT byte $7F reaching glyph 127 (DRF
; ConvertChars - DRB's UTF-8 key-35 table never fires in this
; pipeline), uppercase accents = triples $20-$2F reaching glyphs
; 160-175, uppercase acutes = triples $7B-$7F reaching glyphs 251-255.
; Latin-1 source ON PURPOSE: DRF reads the DSF as Latin-1 and emits
; the triples itself (a UTF-8 source double-converts and fails the
; byte asserts).
;
; Verbs:
;   ACC    reprint the six render lines (E1/E2/SS/MX/UC/UA)
;   PAGE   5-row window + a long accented message - More... paging
;          across pre-shifted buffered words
;   FORCE  MODE 1 window (WIN_FLAGS bit 0), plain text - force-upper
;          shifts EVERY char; MODE 0 restores
;   R      CLS + RESTART - the #g latch and window modes must reset
/CTL
_
/VOC
ACC    10  verb
PAGE   11  verb
FORCE  12  verb
R      24  verb
REDES  24  verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I don't know that verb - try ACC PAGE FORCE R."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 " "
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "E1 áéíóúñÑçÇüÜª¡¿«»#n"
/1 "E2 àãäâèëêìïîòõöôùû#n"
/2 "SS ß#n"
/3 "MX ªàªà#n"
/4 "NEXTDAAD ACCENT FIXTURE#nVERBS  ACC  PAGE  FORCE  R#n"
/5 "ligne une: théâtre français#nligne deux: à bientôt naïve#nligne trois: gruß wörter über#nligne quatre: irmão corações#nligne cinq: noël aïeul où#nligne six: été île pâte#nligne sept: süß hören lärm#nligne huit: fimarduìno tù#nligne neuf: ça irá ñandú#nligne dix: fin des lignes#n"
/6 "FORCED UPPER LINE#n"
/7 "UC ÀÃÄÂÈËÊÌÏÎÒÕÖÔÙÛ#n"
/8 "UA ÁÉÍÓÚ#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The accent lab."
/CON
/0
/1
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
; Banner is one-shot (AT 0 exits via GOTO 1); PROCESS 1 must stay an
; unconditional separate entry (the txt40 fixture precedent).
> _ _   AT 0
        CLS
        MESSAGE 4
        MESSAGE 0
        MESSAGE 1
        MESSAGE 2
        MESSAGE 3
        MESSAGE 7
        MESSAGE 8
        GOTO 1
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _     PARSE 0
          REDO
> ACC   _ MESSAGE 0
          MESSAGE 1
          MESSAGE 2
          MESSAGE 3
          MESSAGE 7
          MESSAGE 8
          DONE
> PAGE  _ WINDOW 2
          WINAT 2 0
          WINSIZE 5 32
          CLS
          MESSAGE 5
          WINDOW 1
          DONE
> FORCE _ MODE 1
          MESSAGE 6
          MODE 0
          DONE
> R     _ CLS
          RESTART
> _ _     NEWTEXT
          SYSMESS 8
          REDO
/END
